  "methodology": "Each sample is a retained BDN Workload/Result iteration's Nanoseconds divided by Operations. One operation is one synthetic authorization chain including the benchmark wrapper, and for suspension cases gate allocation/release/consumption; the layered correlation cases also include AsyncLocal set/restore. Actual, warmup and pilot measurements remain in immutable source exports. Five warmups, twelve target iterations, one launch per configuration and independent wrapper process per pass; the second pass reverses configuration order. The toolchain/process layout is recorded for every run and must match across the accepted study. The standard toolchain uses a generated benchmark child process per workload; an explicitly configured historical in-process fallback shares a wrapper process within a configuration. Passes and families are never pooled. Error is BDN's 99.9% Student-t confidence margin for retained iteration samples, not request latency, a prediction interval, or evidence of independent process replication.",
